{"path":"experimental/shared_future/shared_future","title":"std::experimental::shared_future<T>::shared_future","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::shared_future&lt;T&gt;::</span>shared_future","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/shared_future/shared_future","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">shared_future<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">shared_future<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/shared_future\"><span class=\"kw2813\">std::<span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">shared_future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> f <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">shared_future<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/shared_future\"><span class=\"kw2813\">std::<span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">shared_future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> f <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">shared_future<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/future\"><span class=\"kw2771\">std::<span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/shared_future\"><span class=\"kw2813\">std::<span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">shared_future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_5\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">shared_future<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/future\"><span class=\"kw2771\">std::<span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">future</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> f <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (5) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Default constructor. Constructs an empty <code>shared_future</code> object that does not refer to a shared state.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Constructs a <code>shared_future</code> object, transferring the shared state held by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>, if any. After construction, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f.<span class=\"me1\">valid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> Constructs a shared future that refers to the same shared state as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>, if any.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Unwrapping constructor. Constructs a <code>shared_future</code> object from the shared state referred to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>, if any. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">valid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> prior to this call, the constructed <code>shared_future</code> object is empty. Otherwise, the resulting <code>shared_future</code> object becomes ready when one of the following happens:\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> are both ready. The value or exception from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is stored in the shared state associated with the resulting <code>shared_future</code> object.\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> is ready, but <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is invalid. An exception of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_error\">std::future_error</a></span> with an error condition of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_errc\">std::future_errc::broken_promise</a></span> is stored in the shared state associated with the resulting <code>shared_future</code> object.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\"></span> After this constructor returns, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">valid<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is equal to the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">valid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> prior to this call, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other.<span class=\"me1\">valid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">5)</span> Constructs a <code>shared_future</code> object, transferring the shared state held by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>, if any. After construction, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f.<span class=\"me1\">valid</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> f\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> another future object to initialize with\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a <code>std::experimental::future</code> object to unwrap\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2697\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2697</a>\n</td>\n<td>Concurrency TS\n</td>\n<td>behavior of unwrapping constructor is unclear with an invalid <code>future</code>\n</td>\n<td>constructs an empty <code>future</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/shared_future/shared_future\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs the future object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::shared_future&lt;T&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/shared_future","title":"std::experimental::shared_future"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::shared_future<T>::shared_future","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"5 declarations. Default constructor. Constructs an empty shared_future object that does not refer to a shared state."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"f, other"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs the future object"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":292,"codeBlockCount":0}
